"""
Discord bot that lets you edit the axiomatic prompt files and start/stop the
generation schedule from a Discord channel. The bot only listens to one channel
(CHANNEL_ID); messages elsewhere are ignored.

Commands (case-sensitive prefix, then a space, then the payload):

Prompt editing:
  !prompt_set <text>           Overwrite prompt.md with <text>
  !prompt_append <text>        Append <text> to prompt.md (with a leading newline)
  !prompt_clear                Empty prompt.md
  !prompt_info                 Show prompt.md / todo_character1.md / todo_character2.md
                               in three code blocks

Character todos (Nth = 1, 2):
  !characterN_add <prompt>     Append <prompt> as a new entry to todo_characterN.md
  !characterN_list             Show numbered list of entries in todo_characterN.md
  !characterN_remove <index>   Delete the 1-based entry at <index>
  !characterN_pop              Delete the last entry
  !characterN_clear            Empty todo_characterN.md

Schedule control:
  !run / !start                Start the webrunner (tries webrunner_je_only.py first;
                               on non-zero exit within 5 min auto-falls back to
                               webrunner_novelai.py). One instance at a time.
  !run in 90m | !run at 02:00  Schedule a delayed start (!run cancel to abort)
  !stop                        Stop the running webrunner
  !status                      Report whether the schedule is running, and which variant
  !restart                     Exit the bot; start_discord_bot.py respawns it

Other:
  !help                        Show the command reference (this list)

Token: read from ``discord_bot_token.md`` (entire file content, stripped).

Run:
    py -3 -m pip install discord.py
    py -3 axiomatic/discord_bot.py
"""
